KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicitly instantiated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ extern template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
N5008 [temp.explicit]/12: `extern template int box<int>::put(short);'
suppresses only the implicit instantiation; the program's explicit
instantiation definition defines the same specialization.  The parser
keeps such a declaration of a member function, which becomes a bodiless
member hiding the template ("no body for callee box<int>::put").
Discarding it, as for a free function, fixes this and converts
libstdc++'s basic_ostream::_M_insert without drops, but the faithful
num_put over the unmodelled "C"-locale facets (whose data libstdc++.so
provides) makes cpp11_stream_setw and gcc16_stream_ctype_facet_vtable
time out (the SAT problem exceeds 8 GB).  Pending a model of those
facets.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
